# Exasol Provider

The Exasol provider manages [Exasol](https://www.exasol.com/) database resources with Terraform: users, roles, schemas, external connections, and privileges. It is built on the Terraform Plugin Framework and the official [exasol-driver-go](https://github.com/exasol/exasol-driver-go).

~> **Note** This is an open source project and is **not** officially supported by Exasol.

## Features

- **Users** with `PASSWORD`, `LDAP`, or `OpenID` authentication
- **Roles** and role membership grants
- **Schemas** with optional ownership transfer
- **Connections** to external systems (S3, FTP, JDBC, ...) and connection access grants
- **System and object privileges**
- Full `terraform import` and in-place rename support on every resource

## Authentication

Authenticate with a username and password, or with an Exasol Personal Access Token (PAT). Pass a PAT in the `password` field; tokens prefixed with `exa_pat_` are detected automatically.

For local Exasol containers with a self-signed certificate, set `validate_server_certificate = false`.

